					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-163007#post-4024367</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-163007/scp-2559-j#post-4024367</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 15 Oct 2018 02:05:23 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Mark Penrice</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1858819</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hmm, the comic definitely postdates the SCP, and I wouldn't be surprised at the author being a fan of the foundation&#8230;</p> <p>Anyway, 11.6L/s seems awfully low for something that's meant to have ludicrously high pressure and was able to fill an entire lab in a matter of seconds. If the portal was extremely small, maybe only just large enough to fit a newborn kitten through, then the speed of their passage could be violently fast, but it still remains that even a 1-metre cube holds 1000 litres. My own rather pokey bathroom, which is something like 2 x 2 x 2.5 metres would take around 15 minutes to fill at that rate. Maybe 11.6 cubic metres per second (11.6kL/s) would be more realistic?</p> <p>11.6L/s could almost certainly be dealt with just by mulching the incoming kittens and distributing them amongst various local sewerage systems. 11.6m^3/s would require a much more concentrated global effort, as that's several hundred tonnes of kitten per minute&#8230;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
